# Scenes show, scripts own

The scene is the look. Scripts and `.tres` resources are the game.

## Where state lives

HP, guard, decks, turn order, and rules live on scripts and resources (`MechState`, `CardData`, deck `.tres` files). A label, slider, or button only displays that state. Do not read `Label.text` or a control's value to decide combat, movement, or win conditions.

## How data moves

Managers push data down by calling methods or setting properties on child visuals. UI reports input up with signals (`pressed`, `pulled`, `confirmed`). The parent updates the model, then refreshes the view.

```gdscript
# Bad: the bar polls the model every frame
func _process(_delta: float) -> void:
    value = player.hp

# Good: the model emits; the bar updates when health changes
func _ready() -> void:
    player.health_changed.connect(set_hp)
```

## What may stay on the node

A self-contained control may own its hover, pulse, or reveal animation. `AnimationPlayer` and particle nodes own their playback. Trigger them with a method or signal. Do not step those frames from a manager's `_process`.
